# KNOWN GAP (found R45 Track G while auditing the chain-link postfix axis).
#
# ETry — the postfix `?` — over an `Option[String]`, with a method called on the
# unwrapped result. `infer.gg`'s ETry arm documents the intended semantics:
# "try expr — unwraps Result[T,E] -> T, Option[T] -> T". Both lanes are broken,
# in different ways (Core #8: two bugs).
#
#   RUST gg   : ICE, exit 101 —
#                 [resource-moves] 1 violation(s):
#                   @main::bb0::i4 - shallow copy of resource _5 : Option__GorgetString
#                 panicked at src/ir/lowering/mod.rs: GIR module failed
#                 resource-move validation
#               Same VALIDATOR as the compound-assign ICE family, reached by a
#               different lowering path: the ETry lowering shallow-copies the
#               Option resource instead of borrowing or moving it.
#   SELF-HOST : rejects at resolve — `error[E_UndefinedName]: undefined name
#               `to_upper`` — i.e. it does not resolve a method on the ETry
#               result at all.
#
# CORRECT output is `HI`.
struct Src5:
    int n

equip Src5:
    Option[String] fetch(self):
        return Some("hi")

void main():
    Src5 s = Src5(1)
    print(s.fetch()?.to_upper())
